-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/ba3d2d40-2c03-5f72-8df2-6cf39dbd2ffd
-- title:
--   Reading a non-node place forbids supersingular j (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Further, $W$ is a finite set of places of the level-$M'$ function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A)(M')$ over the residue field $\kappa_A=\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ (a place being a valuation subring containing the base field, proper, and a principal ideal ring), and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ_A`: the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})\in\mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \kappa_A$, where $\mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \Omega$ is the set of $j\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. The inclusion `hle` asserts $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the second field being the geometric function field of level $q^2M'$ with level group `levelH q M'` (a kernel of a reduction map of unit groups).
--
--   Reduction data. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A)(M')$, that is a valuation subring `R₀.integers` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with a place map preserving degrees and matching orders of divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ lies in `R₀.integers`, with residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Also $\zeta$ is an index in $\mathrm{Idx}\ q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and two families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the projective line $\mathrm{ProjLine}\ q$ over $\mathbb Z/q$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   Igusa hypotheses. `hIg_inf` describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\ q)$ as a Gauss ring: $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ after pushing $x,y$ into $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}$. `hIg` says each line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\ q\ \gamma\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}\ q$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\ q)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$; `hIg_inj` says $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta'\ \gamma$ permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   Supersingular-chart hypotheses. `hSS_A` says that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` says: for $s\in W$ and $f\in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}\ j_q$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta'\ \gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr` provides, for each $s$, an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t-a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every constant $a\in A$.
--
--   Prolongation. $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ to the reduced level field $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A)(q^2M')(\mathrm{levelH}\ q\ M')$, i.e. a valuation subring with a surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants; `hR` identifies `R.integers` with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\ q)$ and `hR₀O` says that $f$ lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\ q)$.
--
--   Arithmetic constants. An element $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}\cap A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ is given. Next, $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the contraction $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` asserts that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Also $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le \ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $A_1=A\cap K_1$ (membership characterised elementwise), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The level form $F_0$. Regarding $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ satisfying four conditions: the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$; $F_0$ is stable under every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta'\ \gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness clause, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\ m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\ m\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $k_0(\text{image of }K')$ with $F_0$, if the $c_i$ are linearly independent over $K'$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ then all $a_i=0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The model. Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $k_0(\text{image of }K_1)$ with $F_0$ inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$. An $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ is given, subject to the compatibility that the image of $a\in A_1$ in $T_1$ is the constant $a$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$; $j_1\in T_1$ is a nonzero element whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ is the inclusion of the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}\ j_q$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$. Finally $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is a finite set of places of the reduced level field over $\kappa_A$ for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A)(M')$ to that field such that, first, for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` the image of $f$ lies in `R.integers` with $R$-residue equal to $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and second, $Q\in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ exactly when there is $s\in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$.
--
--   For the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\ A_1\ T_1\ j_1$ — the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{XFin}=\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1]$ and $\mathrm{XInf}=\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$ inside $T_1$ — the following abbreviations are introduced. $\mathrm{InStalk}\ x\ f$ holds when for every point $y$ of $\mathrm{XFin}$ mapping to $x$ under $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ there are $g,h$ in the finite chart algebra with $h\notin y$ and $f h=g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for $\mathrm{XInf}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and the infinite chart algebra; $\mathrm{InMax}\ x\ f$ is the same with the extra requirement $g\in y$ in each clause. $\mathrm{Centred}\ P\ x$, for a place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, requires $P$ to be rational and every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\ x\ f$ to lie in the valuation subring of $P$, to have $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\ f\in A$, and to satisfy $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\ f$ less than $1$ if and only if $\mathrm{InMax}\ x\ f$. $\mathrm{GoodPt}\ x$ conjoins: $x$ lies over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\ A_1$; $x$ is closed, in the form that $x\rightsquigarrow y$ forces $y=x$; for every $y$ in either chart over $x$, every chart element whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; and, for every $y$ in $\mathrm{XFin}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \Omega$. $\mathrm{Reads}\ x\ Q$ requires every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\ x\ f$ to lie in `R.integers`, to have $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, and to have that residue a non-unit there exactly when $\mathrm{InMax}\ x\ f$. $\mathrm{OffBranch}\ x$ requires, for every line $\ell\ne\mathrm{lineInfty}\ q$ and every $y$ in either chart over $x$, a chart element whose image is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ such that $x$ lies over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\ A_1$, $x$ is closed ($x\rightsquigarrow y$ implies $y=x$), and, for every $y$ in $\mathrm{XFin}$ over $x$ and every $y$ in $\mathrm{XInf}$ over $x$, every element of the corresponding chart algebra whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ is a non-unit of `R.integers` belongs to $y$ — and for every place $Q$ of the reduced level field over $\kappa_A$ with $Q\notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and $\mathrm{Reads}\ x\ Q$ — the following holds: for every $y$ in $\mathrm{XFin}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$-image $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin}\ A_1\ T_1\ j_1)$ does not lie in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \Omega$. Thus the hypotheses reproduce the first four clauses of $\mathrm{GoodPt}\ x$ and the conclusion is its last clause; the abbreviations $\mathrm{Centred}$, $\mathrm{GoodPt}$ and $\mathrm{OffBranch}$ occur in the statement as definitions only.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case of the step, on the Igusa leg of the semistable-covering construction for full level structures, which shows that a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and reading a place outside the Igusa nodes cannot have supersingular $j$-invariant. It is used in the assembly of good off-branch reading points, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three).
